WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.190
Bangladesh might just be

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:07.503
the most resilient country on the planet.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:10.800
Once the poorest part of British India,

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.620
it became the most
deprived part of Pakistan

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:17.073
before experiencing the deadliest
cyclone in human history.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:21.060
That was followed by a
liberation war, famine,

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.670
numerous political coups
and assassinations,

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.370
and devastating natural disasters.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:30.030
The important thing is
that we have developed

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.040
our internal capability to cope

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.260
with many of these disasters.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.693
Bangladesh had to do it
for its own survival.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.440
Famously referred to as a "basket case"

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.200
in 1971 by US government officials

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.350
including Henry Kissinger,
in per capita terms,

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:49.650
it's now among the richest
countries in South Asia,

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.933
surpassing India in 2020.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.680
It's not so secret to economic success

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:00.480
is what experts call
RMG, Ready Made Garments.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.060
Every country in the world started

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:07.110
the industrial revolution
with RMG, be it London,

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:11.643
New York, Japan, Korea,
China, and now Bangladesh.

00:01:12.679 --> 00:01:14.100
The need to fill factory floors

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.510
has made a positive impact

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:18.840
on one group in particular, women.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:20.370
And that's set Bangladesh apart

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:23.373
from other Muslim-majority
countries, as well as India.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.790
This is also a component
of the capitalist society

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:29.792
that kind of promotes individualism.

00:01:29.792 --> 00:01:31.500
And that could be one reason

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.230
that a large number of
women came into work.

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:35.880
They did not want to be chained

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:39.993
as a domestic helping
hand to any households.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.690
But Bangladesh might be a victim

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:44.580
of its own success.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:47.250
In 2026, the UN will upgrade it

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.590
from least developed country status,

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:52.920
but this will mean the
loss of economic benefits.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.200
Along with lasting bias towards women,

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.210
Islamic fundamentalist groups,

00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:00.570
and no real plans to move
beyond low-end manufacturing,

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:03.573
the rapid progress of
Bangladesh could be at risk.

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.910
On August 15, 1947,

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.220
the great symbol of the
British empire came down

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:19.590
for the last time to be replaced

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:21.963
by the banner of the
new Indian government.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:28.050
The partition of India
created two dominions

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:31.530
to separate Muslim and
non-Muslim populations,

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.840
India and West and East Pakistan,

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.270
which included modern day Bangladesh.

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:38.700
14 million people were displaced

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.050
because they left their homes.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.940
Anywhere between 1 and 2 million people,

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:44.640
Hindus, Muslims, and Sikhs, they died.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.650
Muslims who had been murdered on the way.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:49.590
Hindus and Sikhs who had
been murdered by Muslims.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:51.120
People of our generation,

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.370
the older generation has almost died out.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:56.103
So that's the very tragic
story of partition.

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:00.300
For over two decades,

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:04.080
the majority Bengali population
in East Pakistan was ruled

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.600
by a central government
based in West Pakistan,

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.873
which spent the majority of
capital on its own development.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:13.380
So the Bengali grievance was that Bengal

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:16.230
was being deprived of its legitimate share

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:18.030
in economic resources.

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:20.730
In the mid 1960s that came to a head

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:23.100
through a demand for regional autonomy,

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:26.040
which we called the six point program.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:29.370
We in Bangladesh called
it our Magna Carta,

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:31.470
because from the six point onward,

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:33.720
we went to one point,
which was independence.

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:38.790
But before obtaining independence,

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:43.230
in 1970 the deadliest cyclone
in human history took place

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:45.933
in which up to 500,000 people died.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:50.070
There was no response from
the Pakistan government,

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:52.320
no measures toward rehabilitation,

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.800
toward coming to the aid
of those who had survived,

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.480
coming to locate the bodies

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.630
or calculate the damage
that had been done.

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:05.250
This accelerated the call for independence

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:08.067
and during the first democratic
election in Pakistan,

00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:09.750
the Awami League Party led

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:13.470
by Sheikh Mujibur Rahman
won a decisive majority.

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:14.790
Legally I am the authority

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:17.010
because people have voted to me.

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:18.720
Now they are using their force,

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:20.923
it's up to them now to decide what to do.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:24.810
Not wanting Pakistan to
be ruled from the East,

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:25.770
the central government

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:28.083
in West Pakistan took military action.

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:30.840
On the 25th of March,

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:33.780
the Pakistan army launched
what has come to be known

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:35.790
as Operation Searchlight.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:39.240
It's estimated that on
the very first night

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:42.120
between 5,000 and 7,000 people were killed

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:43.770
on the streets of Dhaka

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:47.250
and in the course of
more than nine months,

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:50.310
the estimates put out by
the government of Bangladesh

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:52.803
is that 3 million people were killed.

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:57.090
The killings, which
Bangladesh calls genocide,

00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:58.680
were followed by a liberation war

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:01.050
between East and West Pakistan.

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:03.120
10 million refugees fled to India

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:04.770
while the massacres continued

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:07.200
and hundreds of thousands died.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.690
It was India that came to the rescue.

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:12.150
An India-Bangladesh
joint command was formed

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:15.240
and very briskly, very
swiftly, they conquered,

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:17.790
they captured ever larger
slices of territory

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:19.050
in East Pakistan.

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:22.830
And that was when The People's
Republic of Bangladesh

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:23.970
was born.

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:26.460
Although Bangladesh was newly independent,

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:29.640
after years of turmoil, it
was the second poorest nation

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:30.660
in the world.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.410
And things were about to get worse.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.260
Industries are at a halt,

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:40.470
paraffin needed for cooking
and heating is very scarce.

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:42.630
And huge queues form for any supplies

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:43.833
that becomes available.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:47.130
In its first four years,

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:50.370
the newly independent nation
was plagued by mismanagement

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:52.980
and food shortages led
to a disastrous famine

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:56.880
in which an estimated
1.5 million people died.

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:59.790
But then the tragedy,
again, another tragedy,

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:01.170
Sheikh Mujibur was assassinated

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:03.540
by a group of junior military officers.

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:05.823
He and most of his family were killed.

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:16.110
Despite political instability,

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:18.000
coups and assassinations,

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.420
the '80s saw rapid economic improvements.

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:23.610
There has been a sequence of reforms

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:26.250
that has initiated the private sector-led

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:29.190
growth in Bangladesh.

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:31.664
We have to keep in mind
that Bangladesh has started

00:06:31.664 --> 00:06:33.000
as a socialist country.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:35.670
It nationalized everything from banks

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:39.180
to all kinds of factories,
manufacturing and so on.

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:41.160
The outcome was not very good.

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:43.860
And the government realized it

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:47.910
and slowly started going
back to the market mechanism,

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:49.770
allowed the private sector to come in,

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:51.960
which is the most important thing.

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:54.540
At the same time,
positive changes initiated

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:57.210
by NGOs were embraced by the government.

00:06:57.210 --> 00:06:59.370
Like BRAC, a nonprofit created

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:02.190
to help those in need
after the Liberation War.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:05.190
And Grameen Bank, the
so-called bank for the poor.

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:06.960
It gives millions in small loans

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:09.990
to the impoverished without
requiring collateral.

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:12.663
97% of its borrowers are women.

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:14.790
Bangladesh being one

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:17.610
of the poorest countries in the world,

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:21.090
it was also a ground for experimentation

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:22.830
for social development.

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:26.280
This NGO sector, supported
by the government

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:28.590
and also the international community.

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:32.850
I must say that that donor
community played a big role

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:37.530
in supporting the drive that
was led with the government.

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:41.730
And the result is that in
a lot of social innovation,

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:46.410
social engineering,
Bangladesh has pioneered

00:07:46.410 --> 00:07:50.220
and established credible
records for development

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:54.390
which is being experimented
or applied in parts of Africa,

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:56.520
Latin America, and other countries.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:59.643
This is something that we feel proud of.

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:04.470
Although foreign aid played a big role

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:06.000
in the development of Bangladesh,

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:09.000
accounting for up to 8% of
their Gross National Income

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.903
in the 70s, it's now less than 2%.

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:17.460
Life expectancy has jumped
from 47 to 73 years.

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:20.790
Bangladesh's female literacy
rate is higher than India's,

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:23.373
while its infant mortality rate is lower.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:27.210
Compared with the birth rate
of a Muslim majority country,

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:29.490
even compared with
India, we are better off.

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:31.740
Our birth rate has come down.

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:33.780
Family planning has been adapted

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:36.750
at every family level in
Bangladesh, more or less,

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:38.310
and there is no taboo about it.

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:40.800
There is no religious barrier against it.

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:41.700
Why?

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:44.130
Because of the NGO movement,
because of awareness,

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:47.910
because of government's role
in that also donor support.

00:08:47.910 --> 00:08:52.860
USA has played a very
significant role in popularizing

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:55.620
what I call family planning in Bangladesh.

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:58.770
So we have to admit that the
international community's role,

00:08:58.770 --> 00:09:02.580
domestic effort, and the
government all work together

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:04.198
to bring about the changes.

00:09:04.198 --> 00:09:08.580
And that's why Bangladesh's
population now is almost

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:10.173
at the replacement level.

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:14.760
Another significant shift

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:17.763
for Bangladesh was the birth
of a new local industry.

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:22.290
Inspired by the success of
countries like Vietnam and China

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:24.120
in exporting clothes abroad,

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:26.550
Bangladesh began to
build its own factories,

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:29.043
creating a new entrepreneurial class.

00:09:31.890 --> 00:09:35.283
It's the low-cost starting point

00:09:35.283 --> 00:09:36.960
because Bangladeshis didn't have capital.

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:38.220
We are not a capital rich country.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:41.340
It didn't have the rich upper
class and so on, so forth.

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:43.200
So most of them came

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:45.480
from very ordinary middle class background

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:49.770
and became entrepreneurs,
became self-made entrepreneurs.

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:54.770
It started like a very
small enterprise operation

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:59.433
and now they are big time
players and supplying globally.

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:08.040
I started the garment factory,

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:12.010
very small garment
factory in city centers.

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:13.427
Now, of course Viyellatex Group is one

00:10:13.427 --> 00:10:14.430
of the very renowned groups.

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:17.160
We have almost 15,000 workforce.

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:18.750
I'm sure it is very surprising

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:20.070
that we are designing product

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:21.630
for the top brands in the world.

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:22.470
Everything we do,

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:24.840
that means not only the
garment manufacturing,

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:26.098
the entire process,

00:10:26.098 --> 00:10:29.340
we call ourself end-to-end
solution providers.

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:32.460
We have six, seven garment
manufacturing plants.

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:37.230
We produce roughly 3 million
knit garments every month

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:40.593
and more than 1.5 million
woven shirts every month.

00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:44.070
Today the garment industry accounts

00:10:44.070 --> 00:10:47.193
for up to 80% of the
country's total exports.

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:51.360
Part of the its success is
due to government initiatives

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:53.610
like the Export Development Fund.

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:56.850
Created in 1989, it
allows exporters to borrow

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:58.353
at lower interest rates.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:03.450
And Bangladesh's status as a
LDC or least developed country,

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:05.970
gives it tax-free access
to European markets

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:07.983
to boost trade and economic growth.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:13.560
Also, as China moves away
from low-end manufacturing

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.780
and towards higher-end products like cars,

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:17.883
Bangladesh has been able to benefit.

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:21.090
But perhaps the biggest beneficiaries

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:22.980
of the garment industry are women,

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:26.193
who had previously been unable
to make dependable salaries.

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:29.250
When this garment business started,

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:32.130
somehow we're able to attract these women

00:11:32.130 --> 00:11:33.810
or female workforce to our industry,

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:35.880
and that can help significantly

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:38.640
to improve our, I mean, society.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:42.810
Just imagine, I mean more
than 5 million workforce,

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:44.043
3 million are women.

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:47.730
Average salaries for workers

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:49.440
in the Ready Made Garments industry

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:51.450
are double the country's minimum wage,

00:11:51.450 --> 00:11:54.423
which means that women can
become financially independent.

00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:57.810
In the rural areas,

00:11:57.810 --> 00:12:01.020
there were not that much
employment available.

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:04.980
So the women, they took
off from the rural areas

00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:08.310
that know they need to
search for better employment.

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:11.040
Another sociological thing
is that the emancipation

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:13.890
that they could live by themselves.

00:12:13.890 --> 00:12:16.350
Even though their salary was quite meager,

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:18.540
they also have their mind of their own.

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:21.630
If they were working
within someone's house,

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:23.730
they did not have any vacation,

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:28.380
no festival bonus given, no policies.

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:30.330
At least in the garment sector,

00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:33.060
gradually the policies came into place

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:38.033
so they could get a bonus,
overtime and health security

00:12:38.033 --> 00:12:39.363
and other issues.

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:42.600
High rate of participation in Bangladesh

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:47.130
could be correlated with the
free education for girls.

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:50.130
At the secondary level,
free stipend is given.

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:53.850
We have a very strong
NGO-based communities

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:57.597
and the civil society who
actually looked into this

00:12:57.597 --> 00:13:01.143
and encouraged women's participation.

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:06.930
Since first serving as
Prime Minister in 1996,

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:09.870
Sheikh Hasina, daughter of
the first elected president

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:12.330
of Bangladesh, has also introduced laws

00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:14.630
to balance out the
treatment of men and women.

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:18.690
When Hasina Sheikh came into power,

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:22.080
she herself, took a lot of positive steps

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:25.740
for women's empowerment,
particularly involving women

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:28.050
in income generating activities,

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:32.130
encouraging women to
remain in the RMG sectors

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:35.730
and provided lot of
facilities like daycares.

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:38.730
She actually was the first prime minister

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:41.160
that introduced the national policies

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:45.000
for the advancement of women in 1997.

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:48.480
And there actually, she
directly mentioned in the policy

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:51.750
that women should be
given equal inheritance

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:53.700
to property rights.

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:56.160
But even though great
progress has been made,

00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:59.580
women in Bangladesh are
still not treated as equals.

00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:03.120
Women are still seen as
the second class citizen,

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:06.810
the way the patriarchal
society and the men

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:10.170
and the society family,
and the state perceives

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:12.750
is that women need to be controlled.

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:14.160
There are very few women

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:16.440
in the highest level of decision making,

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:19.080
even in the administrative sector.

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:23.520
Even in the police, navy, military,

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:26.193
women are actually at the
bottom of the hierarchy.

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:31.290
There are also religious
parties in the country

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:33.810
that demand the imposition of Islamic laws

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:35.430
which would threaten the rights of women,

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.683
and the economy that
depends on them to work.

00:14:39.090 --> 00:14:41.850
So even though the religious preachers,

00:14:41.850 --> 00:14:45.300
they say things about
certain rules and norms

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:50.300
and customs women have to follow
when they go now for work.

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:55.080
They have never said that
like broadly in a wider form,

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:58.432
that women cannot work and Bangladesh,

00:14:58.432 --> 00:15:02.398
it's of course, the
secularism, this pillar of,

00:15:02.398 --> 00:15:05.313
one of the strongest
pillar of our constitution.

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:08.310
While a thriving industry

00:15:08.310 --> 00:15:11.670
has helped grow Bangladesh's
economy and empower women,

00:15:11.670 --> 00:15:15.930
a big problem remains:
abysmal working conditions.

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:18.750
Of course, along the way,
there've been tragedies

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:20.460
for example, a few years ago,

00:15:20.460 --> 00:15:22.950
there was called this Rana Plaza tragedy.

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:25.110
There have been fires taking place,

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:27.180
occurring in other garment industries.

00:15:27.180 --> 00:15:30.480
So those have been
accidents, tragic accidents,

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:32.610
which we as a nation regret

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:35.010
and which we feel will
not be happening anymore.

00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:38.010
After the Rana Plaza tragedy

00:15:38.010 --> 00:15:40.110
where over 1000 people died,

00:15:40.110 --> 00:15:43.380
nearly 200 international
brands signed an agreement

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:46.110
that allowed for legally
binding safety commitments,

00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:48.510
independent inspections at the factories,

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:50.520
and contributions for safety training

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:52.560
and factory improvements.

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:55.383
A renewal agreement was signed in 2021.

00:16:02.070 --> 00:16:05.400
The garment industry has been a boost

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:06.960
for Bangladesh's economy.

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:10.500
I think we got the idea of improving,

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:12.960
of going on to other areas,

00:16:12.960 --> 00:16:15.960
and of course, exporting our goods abroad.

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:18.780
So we have our sense of optimism there.

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:21.430
But then again, we're very
cautious about the future.

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:25.560
Exporting abroad could now be easier

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:28.350
with the recent completion
of the Padma Bridge,

00:16:28.350 --> 00:16:30.030
now the longest in Bangladesh

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:32.100
that links the less developed Southwest

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:34.020
with the rest of the country.

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:36.660
It offers a faster route
to the second largest port

00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:38.343
for exporters shipping to Europe.

00:16:39.510 --> 00:16:41.730
If you put a ladder and climb it up,

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:43.944
as development goes up,

00:16:43.944 --> 00:16:46.310
we are still in the
first step of the ladder.

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:51.250
We have not yet broadened the export base

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:53.550
to move up the ladder.

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:56.550
We needed to move to light engineering.

00:16:56.550 --> 00:16:59.340
We needed to move to electronics.

00:16:59.340 --> 00:17:02.160
Government should play the enabling role

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:06.720
and make the playing field
even for all sectors,

00:17:06.720 --> 00:17:08.782
not only for the garments.

00:17:08.782 --> 00:17:13.765
If they can do that, I
think we can see the winners

00:17:13.765 --> 00:17:17.748
which will come out of the market forces.

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:21.510
As Bangladesh graduates

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:23.580
from Least Developed Country status,

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:25.950
the loss of economic
benefits will put pressure

00:17:25.950 --> 00:17:27.390
on its economy.

00:17:27.390 --> 00:17:30.390
Unless the government can sign
tariff-free trade agreements,

00:17:30.390 --> 00:17:33.180
tackle corruption and
diversify its economy,

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:35.370
the goal of reaching
upper-middle income status

00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:37.563
by 2031 may not be met.

